  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Nurseries for Youth Development Project (NYDP): From tree nurseries to implemented farm forestry and afforestation</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">KENAFF addresses farm forestry and reforestation challenges in the context of its Farm Forestry and Afforestation Programme (2021-2030). The AHA and KENAFF cooperation, through KENAFF county associations, establishes up to 20 youth-led tree nurseries in 6 selected counties. The target customers for quality planting material shall be local farmers, local administrators, government institutions, NGOs, and civil society organizations, involved in forestry measures. The project includes capacity building, establishing up to 20 tree nurseries and promoting sustainable practices. Workshops and training programs cover topics such as agroforestry, nursery management, biodiversity conservation, etc. The nurseries serve as centers of excellence and generate income for KENAFF county associations. The project aligns with the national goal of achieving 30% tree cover by 2032 and it contributes to climate adaptation and resilience.</narrative>
  </description>
